<title>USA: Unimed says FDA lifts limit on NTZ study.</title>
<headline>Unimed says FDA lifts limit on NTZ study.</headline>
<dateline>BUFFALO GROVE, Ill. 1996-10-15</dateline>
<text>
<p>Unimed Pharmaceuticals Inc said the U.S. Food and Drug Administration authorized expanded access to the company's nitazoxanide for AIDS patients suffering from cryptosporidiosis.</p>
<p>The expanded access lifts a 150-patient limit that had been imposed on an FDA-approved compassionate use program to make the drug available to AIDS patients suffering from cryptosporidial diarrhea.</p>
<p>&quot;There is no longer a limit on the number of patients,&quot; said the company, which plans to begin a Phase II/III study with the drug, known as NTZ, before year end.</p>
<p>--Chicago Newsdesk 312-408-8787</p>
